keenable.snippet:
Chief facility operator means the [person](https://law.cornell.edu/definitions/index.php?width=840&height=800&iframe=true&def_id=1750a857971ca427b602b040489ce3e7&term_occur=999&term_src=Title:40:Chapter:I:Subchapter:C:Part:52:Subpart:A:52.46) in direct charge and control of the operation of a municipal waste combustor and who is responsible for daily onsite supervision, technical direction, management, and overall performance of the facility.

(i) Records showing the names of the municipal waste combustor [chief facility operator](https://law.cornell.edu/definitions/index.php?width=840&height=800&iframe=true&def_id=9d243600012cdba8b2844aae4ba68bbf&term_occur=999&term_src=Title:40:Chapter:I:Subchapter:C:Part:52:Subpart:A:52.46), [shift supervisors](https://law.cornell.edu/definitions/index.php?width=840&height=800&iframe=true&def_id=781f44c6661fe1bc70ba5da38c4c926f&term_occur=999&term_src=Title:40:Chapter:I:Subchapter:C:Part:52:Subpart:A:52.46), and control room operators who have been provisionally certified by the American Society of Mechanical Engineers or an equivalent State-approved certification program as required by [40 CFR 60.54b](https://www.law.cornell.edu/cfr/text/40/60.54b)(a) including the dates of initial and renewal certifications and documentation of current certification;
(ii) Records showing the names of the municipal waste combustor chief facility operator, shift supervisors, and control room operators who have been fully certified by the American Society of Mechanical Engineers or an equivalent State-approved certification program as required by [40 CFR 60.54b](https://www.law.cornell.edu/cfr/text/40/60.54b)(b) including the dates of initial and renewal certifications and documentation of current certification;
(iii) Records showing the names of the municipal waste combustor chief facility operator, shift supervisors, and control room operators who have completed the EPA municipal waste combustor operator training course or a State-approved equiv

